      "proposition": "The majority will hold that Colorado's non-discrimination mandate is not generally applicable under Employment Division v. Smith because the state permits secular exemptions (such as for low-income or disabled students) while denying religious accommodations, thereby triggering and failing strict scrutiny."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The Court will apply a broad rule that any categorical or discretionary secular exemption to a non-discrimination policy renders the law not generally applicable under Smith, requiring strict scrutiny for religious objectors without needing to show explicit hostility."
